    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d154">

                <pb facs="0312" n="280" xml:id="pg280"/>

                <head>154. Note From the Secretary of State to the President<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d154-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1957-02-26"><hi rendition="#italic">February 26,
                        1957</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. President</hi>: Here is the most recent
                    draft of resolution, which was cabled up to Lodge last night,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d154-f2"/> and also a hastily dictated memorandum indicating roughly
                    our present position.</p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">John Foster Dulles</hi><anchor n="3"
                            xml:id="d154-f3"/></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d154-a1.xml" xpointer="d154-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d154-a2.xml" xpointer="d154-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d154-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d154-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 320/2–2657. Secret. A marginal
                    notation on the source text reads: “Mollet &amp; Pineau saw”. Mollet visited
                    Washington February 26–27. Documentation concerning his visit is <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ibid.</hi>, Conference Files: Lot 62 D 181, CF 833A.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d154-f2" n="2" xml:id="d154-f2-content">
                <p>According to Gadel 154 to USUN, February 26, the text of the draft resolution was
                    telephoned and not cabled to Lodge during the evening of February 25. (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ibid.</hi>, 674.84A/2–2657)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d154-f3" n="3" xml:id="d154-f3-content">
                <p>Printed from a copy that bears this typed signature.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
